Learnt about Array.sort() method. It sorts an unsorted array and stores it in the same variable. It doesn't require or need extra variable to save the sorted array. 
Time complexity of this method: O(nlog n)
Solution of the problem:

class Solution {
    public boolean containsDuplicate(int[] nums) {
        Arrays.sort(nums); // Doesn't require another variable. It simply sorts within nums. Now the nums has the sorted array.
        boolean b=false;

        for(int i=0,j=1; i<nums.length-1 && j<nums.length; i++,j++){
            if(nums[i]==nums[j]){
                b=true;
                return b;
            }
        }

        return b;
    }
}
